            "authorAssociation": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Right now the suggested approach is to utilize `content.sort` to modify which notifications will be shown. As it technically [has complete control over what and in which order can be shown](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/2e2931b3822bf357d2f69cbc0bcb2d99a3f0d4c8/doc/mini-notify.txt#L136-L139).\r\n\r\nOne downside is that it has to rely only on what is [supplied](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/2e2931b3822bf357d2f69cbc0bcb2d99a3f0d4c8/doc/mini-notify.txt#L65-L73), and realistically it is only message and level (as the only documented inputs to `vim.notify()`).\r\n\r\nHere is what I currently have [to not show \"Diagnosing...\" notifications from `lua_ls`](https://github.com/echasnovski/nvim/blob/06e32c2ad6493815c09d8dbb2e3042aa0eee086f/init.lua#L36-L45).",
            "bodyHTML": "<p dir=\"auto\">Right now the suggested approach is to utilize <code class=\"notranslate\">content.sort</code> to modify which notifications will be shown. As it technically <a href=\"https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/2e2931b3822bf357d2f69cbc0bcb2d99a3f0d4c8/doc/mini-notify.txt#L136-L139\">has complete control over what and in which order can be shown</a>.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">One downside is that it has to rely only on what is <a href=\"https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/2e2931b3822bf357d2f69cbc0bcb2d99a3f0d4c8/doc/mini-notify.txt#L65-L73\">supplied</a>, and realistically it is only message and level (as the only documented inputs to <code class=\"notranslate\">vim.notify()</code>).</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Here is what I currently have <a href=\"https://github.com/echasnovski/nvim/blob/06e32c2ad6493815c09d8dbb2e3042aa0eee086f/init.lua#L36-L45\">to not show \"Diagnosing...\" notifications from <code class=\"notranslate\">lua_ls</code></a>.</p>",
            "bodyText": "Right now the suggested approach is to utilize content.sort to modify which notifications will be shown. As it technically has complete control over what and in which order can be shown.\nOne downside is that it has to rely only on what is supplied, and realistically it is only message and level (as the only documented inputs to vim.notify()).\nHere is what I currently have to not show \"Diagnosing...\" notifications from lua_ls.",
